  "system": {
    "identifier": "kuru-black-art-dark-displacement",
    "description": "<p>(As a part of the casting of this Jutsu you must have the Miraigan active.) By focusing your Yin Chakra, you are able to break the instinctual connection of time on a cellular level.</p>\n<p>Make a melee ninjutsu attack, dealing 6d10 Necrotic damage and forcing them to make a Charisma saving throw.</p>\n<p>Critical Success: Affected creatures is able to resist this jutsu’s effects.</p>\n<p>Success: Affected creature is unable to regain hit points until the end of their next turn.</p>\n<p>Failure: Affected creature is unable to regain hit points or chakra points, until the end of your next turn as their cells fail to replicate.</p>\n<p>Critical Failure: Same as failure, but they also cannot maintain concentration on jutsu until the end of your next turn.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above B-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3 and the damage by 1d10.</p>",
